WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Some fish physically fuse

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.667
with their mates.

3
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.167
In the deep sea,

4
00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.500
a tiny male searches

5
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.200
for a much larger female.

6
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:08.333
This is

7
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:09.800
the triplewart seadevil.

8
00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:11.633
He grips her skin

9
00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:12.867
with hooked teeth.

10
00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:14.100
In this species,

11
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.333
attachment becomes permanent.

12
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:16.467
Over time,

13
00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:17.833
their tissues join.

14
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:19.200
Blood vessels connect.

15
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.833
Her blood supplies

16
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:21.667
his nutrients,

17
00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.333
while his testes develop

18
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:24.600
to produce sperm.

19
00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:25.900
He doesn't disappear

20
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.633
into her.

21
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:27.400
He remains

22
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.533
an attached male.

23
00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:29.867
How can foreign

24
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:30.700
tissues coexist?

25
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.300
These fish have lost

26
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.100
key parts

27
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.333
of adaptive immunity.

28
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.767
Exactly how their

29
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.033
remaining defenses work

30
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.767
is still being studied.

31
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.933
In a world

32
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:42.067
where mates are hard to find,

33
00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.433
staying together may secure

34
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:44.167
future spawning.

35
00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.367
Two fish.

36
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.900
A lasting connection.
